     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n**1. The dose is above the usual maximum.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The FDA labeled maximum for prescription ibuprofen is 3200 mg/day, and for most adults the usual maximum is 1200 mg/day OTC or up to 3200 mg/day under medical supervision. A dose this high needs a prescriber to confirm it is intended, and it may be a transcription error (for example, 400 mg or 800 mg QID, or 1600 mg TID or BID).\n\n**2. Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You're not a clinician, so this order should go through the medicine team's prescriber, who can verify the dose against the patient's chart and take responsibility for it.\n\nWhat I'd suggest:\n- Contact the ordering prescriber or the medicine team to confirm the intended dose and frequency.\n- If they confirm a dose above 3200 mg/day is intended, they can enter the order themselves or ask pharmacy to review it.\n- If it helps, I can enter an order once a licensed clinician gives me the confirmed drug, dose, route, and frequency."
      }
     ],
